{"action":"closed","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDAnalysis/mdanalysis/issues/4731","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDAnalysis/mdanalysis","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDAnalysis/mdanalysis/issues/4731/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDAnalysis/mdanalysis/issues/4731/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDAnalysis/mdanalysis/issues/4731/events","html_url":"https://github.com/MDAnalysis/mdanalysis/issues/4731","id":2583629576,"node_id":"I_kwDOAf16f86Z_w8I","number":4731,"title":"Documentation for reconstructing square distance matrix from `self_distance_array` is incorrect. ","user":{"login":"hmacdope","id":24581003,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NTgxMDAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24581003?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope","html_url":"https://github.com/hmacdope","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmacdope/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":195620654,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTU2MjA2NTQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDAnalysis/mdanalysis/labels/defect","name":"defect","color":"fc2929","default":false,"description":null},{"id":195620732,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTU2MjA3MzI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDAnalysis/mdanalysis/labels/Component-Docs","name":"Component-Docs","color":"009800","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2024-10-13T04:15:42Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T17:03:30Z","closed_at":"2024-12-16T17:03:30Z","author_association":"MEMBER","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"The documentation for `self_distance_array` has the following as the suggested way to reconstruct a full NxN distance matrix from the flattened upper triangular (-diagonal) N*(N-2) // 2  result. 

```
for i in range(n):
    for j in range(i + 1, n):
        k += 1
        dist[i, j] = d[k]
```

This is incorrect as the increment must come after the assignment, otherwise you attempt to access N+1 the element of the array on final iteration. 

The below is correct. 

```
for i in range(n):
    for j in range(i + 1, n):
        dist[i, j] = d[k]
        k += 1
```

